{
  "about": "Ask in words, logs (C1762): 20 questions a network engineer types into History › Query › Ask in words (Logs), each with the logs builder's answer expected, decided from the lab's Loki BEFORE any model run (read-only probes on the NMAS host, 2026-10-26 19:22 to 19:26 UTC, through modules/history_logq: `_count`, `window`, `discover`, `mnemonics`, and per-device counts by LOGQL_FIELDS with Mercury's heartbeat exclusion; the network Default's devices r1-r4, r6-r8 (role router) and s1-s5 (role switch); Loki's jobs network_syslog and snmptrapd; the device label since 13 Oct 00:35 UTC, severity since 15 Oct 03:49 UTC). Not yet recorded. `expect` names the logs builder's choices (nl_query.LogsChoices): outcome one of `outcome`; for an answer, the chosen mnemonics equal (as a set) one of the sets in `mnemonics` ([] is no mnemonic), devices exactly `devices` (when given), role `role` (when given), severity one of `severity` (LogsChoices' values: any, or the digit, this level or worse), contains one of `contains` (when given; Loki's |= is case-sensitive, so the case is part of the value; from logs v4 the text is read lower-case and matched in any case, C1834, so it is compared case-folded), contains and excludes both empty when `contains_empty`, show one of `show`, by one of `by` (when show is counts), every one of `every` (when given), range one of `range`, and a named calendar span's From and To by `span` (as metrics.json's, cases._span_misses, in UTC). `evidence` names the Loki count that backs the case and `expect_lines` the lines the expected choices match over the range as measured (a range running to now moves with the clock; `today` and `since Monday` were measured at 19:2x UTC, Monday 26 Oct, when this week and today began at the same midnight). `flag` says what the evidence alone cannot settle, or where the builder as built cannot reach the expected answer. `expect` (cases.logs_misses): outcome one of `outcome`; for an answer, the mnemonics one of the allowed sets in `mnemonics` (order aside; [] none), devices exactly `devices`, role `role`, no text when `contains_empty`, else the text one of `contains`, severity one of `severity` (any for none), show one of `show`, for counts `by` and `every` one of theirs, range one of `range`, and a named `span`. `evidence` and `expect_lines` are what Loki held when the case was written; `cases.stale_logs` checks the expected mnemonics are still offered before any recording.",
